task: reactive-bridge-profile (measurement first; a change only where the count points)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/reactive-bridge-profile

why: the largest ratio measured on 2026-09-06 -- a round trip through
  Flow.Publisher and back reads 5.67x the plain source and 738 bytes
  per element (section 17). Two channels and two demand batches per
  window are in the shape; which of them is the cost was deliberately
  not guessed.

what is visible on reading: Reactive.source builds, PER ELEMENT, an
  Async.Await around c.receiveAsync -- the five-object handshake --
  plus a Writer node and two binds. It does not use receiveMany, which
  Drain uses to take 62 elements per await on the same channel. The
  Pump side is read next.

method: count per side (a wrapping Handler[Async] on the reader; a
  counting Subscriber for onNext/request), then a JFR class breakdown
  of reactiveRound. If the reader's per-element Await is the cost, the
  fix is the reader draining in batches the way `drained` does -- with
  demand still following consumption, refilled per batch. Measured on
  reactiveRound against plainSource; the TCK (39 rules) is the law.
